<AssignMessage name="AM-QuotaKeys">
  <DisplayName>Build the department+user composite quota key</DisplayName>
  <!--
    One shared, use-case-agnostic key: department:oid. It does NOT need to
    know which of /translation, /sales or /naas matched — that separation
    comes for free from WHICH conditional Q-*-DeptUserDay policy fires below
    (each is its own Step, gated on its own path Condition, so it is
    automatically a separate Apigee quota counter regardless of the
    Identifier value). This policy only has to compute the inner
    department+user pair once, so every use case's Tier-3 step can share it
    rather than each recomputing the same string.

    department comes from the plain request header (asserted by the BFF, not
    a verified claim — same trust level as everywhere else on this
    platform, see AM-UserClaims.xml's note on why department is not read
    from the JWT). oid comes from jwt_oid, set by AM-UserClaims from the
    VERIFIED Entra token, so this key is only as trustworthy as its weaker
    half.
  -->
  <AssignVariable>
    <Name>dept_user_key</Name>
    <Template>{request.header.x-colt-user-department}:{jwt_oid}</Template>
  </AssignVariable>
  <IgnoreUnresolvedVariables>true</IgnoreUnresolvedVariables>
</AssignMessage>
